IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc4-part5-assessment`
IMPORT `uc4-part8-ch1-groups`
IMPORT `uc4-part8-ch1-requirements`

-- Part 8 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Chapter 1, regulation 99: the circumstances in which a work search
-- requirement must not be imposed and a work availability requirement is eased.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit (see uc4-seat.l4).
--
-- WHO DECIDES. "The Secretary of State is satisfied", "in the opinion of the Secretary of State" and "specified by the Secretary of
-- State" are stated BOOLEAN inputs or a stated date, worded as the text words them. Where a provision says the Secretary of State "must
-- not impose" a requirement, the rule says whether that is so on the facts given; nothing here imposes anything.
--
-- THE DOTS. Paragraphs (1) and (2) read "(3), (4) , (4A), ... or (6)", and several paragraphs carry a "..." where words were removed
-- from the revised text. The rules read the paragraphs that are named; the dots are not read as naming any other paragraph.

§ `Regulation 99 — Circumstances in which requirements must not be imposed`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph (7) — tribunal`

-- Paragraph (7): "tribunal" means any tribunal listed in Schedule 1 to the Tribunals and Inquiries Act 1992.
-- out of range: Schedule 1 to the Tribunals and Inquiries Act 1992 (not among the inputs): whether the body is listed is a stated input
-- src:1593 | (7) In this regulation “tribunal” means any tribunal listed in Schedule 1 to the Tribunals and Inquiries Act 1992 .
@ref reg 99(7) (src:1593)
GIVEN `the body is listed in Schedule 1 to the Tribunals and Inquiries Act 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(7) — the body is a tribunal` `the body is listed in Schedule 1 to the Tribunals and Inquiries Act 1992` MEANS
    `the body is listed in Schedule 1 to the Tribunals and Inquiries Act 1992`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph (3) — court, prison, treatment, bereavement and public duty`

-- Limb (a): the claimant is attending a court or tribunal as a party to any proceedings or as a witness.
-- out of range: Schedule 1 to the Tribunals and Inquiries Act 1992 (not among the inputs): whether the body is listed is a stated input
-- src:1542 | (3) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:1543 | (a) the claimant is attending a court or tribunal as a party to any proceedings or as a witness;
@ref reg 99(3)(a) (src:1542-1543)
DECLARE `Attendance at a court or tribunal` HAS
    `the claimant is attending a court`                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is attending a tribunal`                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tribunal is listed in Schedule 1 to the Tribunals and Inquiries Act 1992`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is attending as a party to any proceedings`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is attending as a witness`                                                               IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 99(3)(a) (src:1542-1543)
GIVEN attendance IS AN `Attendance at a court or tribunal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(3)(a) — the claimant is attending a court or tribunal as a party or as a witness` attendance MEANS
    `a court or a tribunal`
    AND `a party or a witness`
    WHERE
        `a court or a tribunal` MEANS
            (attendance's `the claimant is attending a court`)
            OR ((attendance's `the claimant is attending a tribunal`) AND (`reg 99(7) — the body is a tribunal` (attendance's `the tribunal is listed in Schedule 1 to the Tribunals and Inquiries Act 1992`)))
        `a party or a witness` MEANS
            (attendance's `the claimant is attending as a party to any proceedings`)
            OR (attendance's `the claimant is attending as a witness`)

-- Limb (b): the claimant is a prisoner (the core's definition of regulation 2).
-- src:1544 | (b) the claimant is a prisoner;
@ref reg 99(3)(b) (src:1544)
GIVEN detention IS A Detention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(3)(b) — the claimant is a prisoner` detention MEANS
    `reg 2 — prisoner` detention

-- Limb (c): regulation 11(3) (temporary absence from Great Britain for treatment or convalescence) applies to the claimant.
-- Regulation 11 is outside this piece's ranges, so whether it applies is a stated input.
-- out of range: regulation 11(3) (piece uc1): whether it applies is a stated input
-- src:1545 | (c) regulation 11(3) (temporary absence from Great Britain for treatment or convalescence) applies to the claimant;
@ref reg 99(3)(c) (src:1545)
GIVEN `regulation 11(3) applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(3)(c) — regulation 11(3) applies to the claimant` `regulation 11(3) applies to the claimant` MEANS
    `regulation 11(3) applies to the claimant`

-- Limb (d): any of the persons listed has died within the past 6 months. "Within the past 6 months" is read as: the death was on or before
-- the date asked about, and that date is before the day 6 months after the death (fork F-99-1, the same reading as regulation 98(2)).
-- out of range: regulation 5 (piece uc1): whether a person is a qualifying young person is a stated input
-- src:1546 | (d) any of the following persons has died within the past 6 months—
-- src:1547 | (i) where the claimant was a member of a couple, the other member,
-- src:1548 | (ii) a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant or, where the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member, was responsible, or
-- src:1549 | (iii) a child, where the claimant was the child's parent;
@ref reg 99(3)(d) (src:1546-1549)
DECLARE `Deaths within the past 6 months` HAS
    `date of death of the other member of the couple, where the claimant was a member of a couple`           IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date of death of a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant or, where the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member, was responsible`   IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date of death of a child, where the claimant was the child's parent`                                  IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref reg 99(3)(d) (src:1546-1549)
GIVEN death IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(3)(d) — a death on this date is within the past 6 months` death `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER death
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST died THEN
        ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day died) AT LEAST 0)
        AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` died (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 6, unit IS months))) LESS THAN 0)

@ref reg 99(3)(d) (src:1546-1549)
GIVEN deaths IS A `Deaths within the past 6 months`
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(3)(d) — any of the following persons has died within the past 6 months` deaths `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    (`reg 99(3)(d) — a death on this date is within the past 6 months` (deaths's `date of death of the other member of the couple, where the claimant was a member of a couple`) `the date as at which it is asked`)
    OR (`reg 99(3)(d) — a death on this date is within the past 6 months` (deaths's `date of death of a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant or, where the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member, was responsible`) `the date as at which it is asked`)
    OR (`reg 99(3)(d) — a death on this date is within the past 6 months` (deaths's `date of death of a child, where the claimant was the child's parent`) `the date as at which it is asked`)

-- Limb (e): the claimant is, and has been for no more than 6 months, receiving and participating in a structured recovery-orientated course
-- of alcohol or drug dependency treatment. "No more than 6 months" runs from the day the course began to the day 6 months later,
-- both inclusive (fork F-99-2).
-- src:1550 | (e) the claimant is, and has been for no more than 6 months, receiving and participating in a structured recovery-orientated course of alcohol or drug dependency treatment;
@ref reg 99(3)(e) (src:1550)
GIVEN `the claimant is receiving and participating in a structured recovery-orientated course of alcohol or drug dependency treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date on which the claimant began receiving and participating in the course` IS A DATE
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(3)(e) — the claimant is in a course of treatment and has been for no more than 6 months` `the claimant is receiving and participating in a structured recovery-orientated course of alcohol or drug dependency treatment` `date on which the claimant began receiving and participating in the course` `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    `the claimant is receiving and participating in a structured recovery-orientated course of alcohol or drug dependency treatment`
    AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day `date on which the claimant began receiving and participating in the course`) AT LEAST 0)
    AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` `date on which the claimant began receiving and participating in the course` (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 6, unit IS months))) AT MOST 0)

-- Limb (f): the claimant is, and has been for no more than 3 months, a person for whom arrangements have been made by a protection
-- provider under section 82 of the Serious Organised Crime and Police Act 2005 (the same reading of "no more than", fork F-99-2).
-- out of range: section 82 of the Serious Organised Crime and Police Act 2005 (not among the inputs): whether arrangements have been made is a stated input
-- src:1551 | (f) the claimant is, and has been for no more than 3 months, a person for whom arrangements have been made by a protection provider under section 82 of the Serious Organised Crime and Police Act 2005 ; or
@ref reg 99(3)(f) (src:1551)
GIVEN `arrangements have been made for the claimant by a protection provider under section 82 of the Serious Organised Crime and Police Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date from which those arrangements have applied to the claimant` IS A DATE
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(3)(f) — the claimant is under protection arrangements and has been for no more than 3 months` `arrangements have been made for the claimant by a protection provider under section 82 of the Serious Organised Crime and Police Act 2005` `date from which those arrangements have applied to the claimant` `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    `arrangements have been made for the claimant by a protection provider under section 82 of the Serious Organised Crime and Police Act 2005`
    AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day `date from which those arrangements have applied to the claimant`) AT LEAST 0)
    AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` `date from which those arrangements have applied to the claimant` (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 3, unit IS months))) AT MOST 0)

-- Limb (g): the claimant is engaged in an activity of a kind approved by the Secretary of State as being in the nature of a public duty.
-- src:1552 | (g) the claimant is engaged in an activity of a kind approved by the Secretary of State as being in the nature of a public duty.
@ref reg 99(3)(g) (src:1552)
GIVEN `the claimant is engaged in an activity of a kind approved by the Secretary of State as being in the nature of a public duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(3)(g) — the claimant is engaged in an activity approved as being in the nature of a public duty` `the claimant is engaged in an activity of a kind approved by the Secretary of State as being in the nature of a public duty` MEANS
    `the claimant is engaged in an activity of a kind approved by the Secretary of State as being in the nature of a public duty`

-- Paragraph (3): applies where any of limbs (a) to (g) is met.
@ref reg 99(3) (src:1542)
GIVEN `limb (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(3) — this paragraph applies` `limb (a)` `limb (b)` `limb (c)` `limb (d)` `limb (e)` `limb (f)` `limb (g)` MEANS
    `limb (a)` OR `limb (b)` OR `limb (c)` OR `limb (d)` OR `limb (e)` OR `limb (f)` OR `limb (g)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraphs (4), (4ZA) and (4ZB) — unfitness for work`

-- Paragraph (4)(a): unfit for work for no more than 14 consecutive days after the date the evidence is provided, and for no more than
-- 2 such periods in any period of 12 months. The claimant must be unfit at all (at least one day); the count of periods in the 12 months
-- includes the present one (fork F-99-3).
-- out of range: Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the Medical Evidence Regulations (not among the inputs): whether a statement was given in accordance with it is a stated input
-- src:1553 | (4) Subject to paragraph (4ZA), this paragraph applies where the claimant—
-- src:1554 | (a) is unfit for work—
-- src:1555 | (i) for a period of no more than 14 consecutive days after the date that the evidence referred to in sub-paragraph (b) is provided, and
-- src:1556 | (ii) for no more than 2 such periods in any period of 12 months; and
@ref reg 99(4)(a) (src:1553-1556)
DECLARE `Unfitness for work facts` HAS
    `days for which the claimant is unfit for work after the date that the evidence referred to in sub-paragraph (b) is provided`   IS A NUMBER
    `number of such periods of unfitness for work in the period of 12 months, including this one`           IS A NUMBER
    `the claimant has provided a declaration, in such manner and form as the Secretary of State approves, that the claimant is unfit for work`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State has requested a statement for those further days`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant has provided a statement given in accordance with the rules set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the Medical Evidence Regulations which provides that the person is not fit for work`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 99(4)(a) (src:1553-1556)
GIVEN facts IS AN `Unfitness for work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(4)(a) — the claimant is unfit for work for a period and number of periods within the limits` facts MEANS
    ((facts's `days for which the claimant is unfit for work after the date that the evidence referred to in sub-paragraph (b) is provided`) AT LEAST 1)
    AND ((facts's `days for which the claimant is unfit for work after the date that the evidence referred to in sub-paragraph (b) is provided`) AT MOST 14)
    AND ((facts's `number of such periods of unfitness for work in the period of 12 months, including this one`) AT MOST 2)

-- Paragraph (4)(b): the evidence. (i) for the first 7 days of unfitness, a declaration. (ii) for any further days, if requested by the
-- Secretary of State, a statement. If no statement is requested, none is needed (fork F-99-4).
-- src:1557 | (b) provides to the Secretary of State the following evidence—
-- src:1558 | (i) for the first 7 days when they are unfit for work, a declaration made by the claimant in such manner and form as the Secretary of State approves that the claimant is unfit for work, and
-- src:1559 | (ii) for any further days when they are unfit for work, if requested by the Secretary of State, a statement given ... in accordance with the rules set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the Medical Evidence Regulations which provides that the person is not fit for work.
@ref reg 99(4)(b)(i) (src:1557-1558)
GIVEN facts IS AN `Unfitness for work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(4)(b)(i) — the claimant has provided a declaration for the first 7 days` facts MEANS
    facts's `the claimant has provided a declaration, in such manner and form as the Secretary of State approves, that the claimant is unfit for work`

@ref reg 99(4)(b)(ii) (src:1559)
GIVEN facts IS AN `Unfitness for work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(4)(b)(ii) — the evidence for any further days has been provided if requested` facts MEANS
    NOT ((facts's `the claimant is unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days`) AND (facts's `the Secretary of State has requested a statement for those further days`) AND (NOT (facts's `the claimant has provided a statement given in accordance with the rules set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the Medical Evidence Regulations which provides that the person is not fit for work`)))

@ref reg 99(4)(b) (src:1557-1559)
GIVEN facts IS AN `Unfitness for work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(4)(b) — the claimant provides the evidence` facts MEANS
    (`reg 99(4)(b)(i) — the claimant has provided a declaration for the first 7 days` facts)
    AND (`reg 99(4)(b)(ii) — the evidence for any further days has been provided if requested` facts)

-- Paragraph (4ZB)(a)(i): it has previously been determined, on the basis of an assessment under Part 5 or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA
-- Regulations, that the claimant does not have limited capability for work.
-- Paragraph (4ZB)(a)(ii): the claimant has previously been treated as not having limited capability for work or, as the case may be, for
-- work and work-related activity, under regulation 43(3) or 44(2). Those rules return the determination the claimant was treated as not
-- satisfying; a treatment as to the severe conditions criteria is not one of the two the paragraph names.
-- src:1560 | (4ZA) Where paragraph (4ZB) applies, paragraph (4) will only apply to a claimant if the Secretary of State makes a decision to carry out an assessment under regulation 41(1)(b).
-- src:1561 | (4ZB) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:1562 | (a) (i) it has previously been determined on the basis of an assessment under Part 5 of these Regulations or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant does not have limited capability for work; or
-- src:1563 | (ii) the claimant has previously been treated as not having limited capability for work or, as the case may be, for work and work-related activity under regulation 43(3) or 44(2); and
@ref reg 99(4ZB)(a)(i) (src:1562)
GIVEN previous IS A `Previous determinations`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(4ZB)(a)(i) — it has previously been determined that the claimant does not have limited capability for work` previous MEANS
    previous's `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant does not have limited capability for work`

@ref reg 99(4ZB)(a)(ii) (src:1563)
GIVEN treated IS A MAYBE `Determination in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(4ZB)(a)(ii) — the claimant has previously been treated as not having limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity` treated MEANS
    CONSIDER treated
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST determination THEN
        CONSIDER determination
        WHEN `whether the claimant has limited capability for work` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `whether the claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `whether the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant` THEN FALSE

-- Paragraph (4ZB)(b): the condition specified in the evidence provided under (4)(b) is in the opinion of the Secretary of State the same,
-- or substantially the same, as the condition specified in the evidence provided before the determination or the treatment.
-- src:1564 | (b) the condition specified in the evidence provided by the claimant in accordance with paragraph (4)(b) is in the opinion of the Secretary of State the same, or substantially the same, as the condition specified in the evidence provided by the claimant before the date—
-- src:1565 | (i) of the determination that the claimant does not have limited capability for work; or
-- src:1566 | (ii) that the claimant was treated as not having limited capability for work or, as the case may be, for work and work-related activity.
@ref reg 99(4ZB) (src:1561-1566)
GIVEN previous IS A `Previous determinations`
      treated IS A MAYBE `Determination in question`
      `in the opinion of the Secretary of State the condition specified in the evidence provided by the claimant in accordance with paragraph (4)(b) is the same, or substantially the same, as the condition specified in the evidence provided by the claimant before the date of the determination or of the treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(4ZB) — this paragraph applies` previous treated `in the opinion of the Secretary of State the condition specified in the evidence provided by the claimant in accordance with paragraph (4)(b) is the same, or substantially the same, as the condition specified in the evidence provided by the claimant before the date of the determination or of the treatment` MEANS
    `previously determined or treated`
    AND `in the opinion of the Secretary of State the condition specified in the evidence provided by the claimant in accordance with paragraph (4)(b) is the same, or substantially the same, as the condition specified in the evidence provided by the claimant before the date of the determination or of the treatment`
    WHERE
        `previously determined or treated` MEANS
            (`reg 99(4ZB)(a)(i) — it has previously been determined that the claimant does not have limited capability for work` previous)
            OR (`reg 99(4ZB)(a)(ii) — the claimant has previously been treated as not having limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity` treated)

-- Paragraph (4ZA): where paragraph (4ZB) applies, paragraph (4) applies only if the Secretary of State makes a decision to carry out an
-- assessment under regulation 41(1)(b).
@ref reg 99(4ZA) (src:1560)
GIVEN `paragraph (4ZB) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State makes a decision to carry out an assessment under regulation 41(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(4ZA) — paragraph (4) is open to the claimant` `paragraph (4ZB) applies` `the Secretary of State makes a decision to carry out an assessment under regulation 41(1)(b)` MEANS
    (NOT `paragraph (4ZB) applies`)
    OR `the Secretary of State makes a decision to carry out an assessment under regulation 41(1)(b)`

-- Paragraph (4): applies where the claimant meets (a) and (b), subject to paragraph (4ZA).
@ref reg 99(4) (src:1553-1559)
GIVEN facts IS AN `Unfitness for work facts`
      `paragraph (4ZB) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State makes a decision to carry out an assessment under regulation 41(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(4) — this paragraph applies` facts `paragraph (4ZB) applies` `the Secretary of State makes a decision to carry out an assessment under regulation 41(1)(b)` MEANS
    (`reg 99(4)(a) — the claimant is unfit for work for a period and number of periods within the limits` facts)
    AND (`reg 99(4)(b) — the claimant provides the evidence` facts)
    AND (`reg 99(4ZA) — paragraph (4) is open to the claimant` `paragraph (4ZB) applies` `the Secretary of State makes a decision to carry out an assessment under regulation 41(1)(b)`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraphs (4A) to (4C) — events affecting a child`

-- Paragraph (4A)(a) and (b): the events. (a) the death of a person who was previously the responsible carer of the child, a parent, a
-- brother or sister, or any other person who normally lived in the same accommodation as the child and was not liable to make payments
-- on a commercial basis in respect of it; (b) the child has been the victim of, or witness to, an incident of violence or abuse and the
-- claimant is not the perpetrator.
-- src:1568 | (a) any of the following persons has died—
-- src:1569 | (i) a person who was previously the responsible carer of that child;
-- src:1570 | (ii) a parent of that child;
-- src:1571 | (iii) a brother or sister of that child; or
-- src:1572 | (iv) any other person who, at the time of their death, normally lived in the same accommodation as that child and was not a person who was liable to make payments on a commercial basis in respect that accommodation; or
-- src:1573 | (b) the child has been the victim of, or witness to, an incident of violence or abuse and the claimant is not the perpetrator of that violence or abuse.
@ref reg 99(4A)(a) and (b) (src:1568-1573)
DECLARE `Event affecting a child in the claimant's care` HAS
    `date of the event`                                                                                    IS A DATE
    `the claimant is the responsible carer of a child`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a person who was previously the responsible carer of that child has died`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `a parent of that child has died`                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `a brother or sister of that child has died`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `any other person who, at the time of their death, normally lived in the same accommodation as that child has died`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `that other person was liable to make payments on a commercial basis in respect of that accommodation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child has been the victim of, or witness to, an incident of violence or abuse`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is the perpetrator of that violence or abuse`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the event has resulted in significant disruption to the claimant's normal childcare responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 99(4A)(a) (src:1568-1572)
GIVEN event IS AN `Event affecting a child in the claimant's care`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(4A)(a) — a person has died` event MEANS
    (event's `a person who was previously the responsible carer of that child has died`)
    OR (event's `a parent of that child has died`)
    OR (event's `a brother or sister of that child has died`)
    OR `another person who lived with the child`
    WHERE
        `another person who lived with the child` MEANS
            (event's `any other person who, at the time of their death, normally lived in the same accommodation as that child has died`)
            AND (NOT (event's `that other person was liable to make payments on a commercial basis in respect of that accommodation`))

@ref reg 99(4A)(b) (src:1573)
GIVEN event IS AN `Event affecting a child in the claimant's care`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(4A)(b) — the child has been a victim of or witness to violence or abuse` event MEANS
    (event's `the child has been the victim of, or witness to, an incident of violence or abuse`)
    AND (NOT (event's `the claimant is the perpetrator of that violence or abuse`))

-- Paragraph (4A): the claimant is the responsible carer of a child and an event in (a) or (b) has taken place in the last 24 months and
-- has resulted in significant disruption to the claimant's normal childcare responsibilities. The event is "in the last 24 months" when
-- it was on or before the date asked about and that date is before the day 24 months after it (fork F-99-1).
-- src:1567 | (4A) This paragraph applies for one or more periods of one month, as provided for in paragraphs (4B) and (4C), where the claimant is the responsible carer of a child and an event referred to in sub-paragraph (a) or (b) has taken place in the last 24 months and has resulted in significant disruption to the claimant’s normal childcare responsibilities—
@ref reg 99(4A) (src:1567)
GIVEN event IS AN `Event affecting a child in the claimant's care`
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(4A) — the circumstances for a period of one month` event `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    (event's `the claimant is the responsible carer of a child`)
    AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day (event's `date of the event`)) AT LEAST 0)
    AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` (event's `date of the event`) (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 24, unit IS months))) LESS THAN 0)
    AND (event's `the event has resulted in significant disruption to the claimant's normal childcare responsibilities`)
    AND `a death or an incident`
    WHERE
        `a death or an incident` MEANS
            (`reg 99(4A)(a) — a person has died` event)
            OR (`reg 99(4A)(b) — the child has been a victim of or witness to violence or abuse` event)

-- Paragraph (4B): not more than one period of one month in each of the 4 consecutive periods of 6 months following the event. The window
-- of a date counts the 6-month boundaries after the event that it has reached: 0 for the first 6 months, up to 3 for the fourth. A date
-- 24 months or more after the event is in no window. The sentence about running concurrently with a period under regulation 98 or
-- paragraph (3)(d) says that the months overlap; it does not move a start date, so no rule here reads it (fork F-99-5).
-- src:1574 | (4B) Paragraph (4A) is not to apply for more than one period of one month in each of the 4 consecutive periods of 6 months following the event (and, if regulation 98 or paragraph (3)(d) of this regulation applies in respect of the same event, that month is to run concurrently with any period for which that regulation or paragraph applies).
@ref reg 99(4B) (src:1574)
GIVEN event IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 99(4B) — the number of the 6-month window after the event in which a day falls` event day MEANS
    (IF ((Day day MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` event (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 6, unit IS months))) AT LEAST 0) THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF ((Day day MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` event (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 12, unit IS months))) AT LEAST 0) THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF ((Day day MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` event (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 18, unit IS months))) AT LEAST 0) THEN 1 ELSE 0)

@ref reg 99(4B) (src:1574)
GIVEN event IS A DATE
      `day on which a further period of one month would begin` IS A DATE
      `days on which earlier periods of one month in respect of the same event began` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(4B) — a period of one month beginning on this day is allowed` event `day on which a further period of one month would begin` `days on which earlier periods of one month in respect of the same event began` MEANS
    ((Day `day on which a further period of one month would begin` MINUS Day event) AT LEAST 0)
    AND ((Day `day on which a further period of one month would begin` MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` event (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 24, unit IS months))) LESS THAN 0)
    AND (NOT (any (GIVEN earlier YIELD (`reg 99(4B) — the number of the 6-month window after the event in which a day falls` event earlier) EQUALS (`reg 99(4B) — the number of the 6-month window after the event in which a day falls` event `day on which a further period of one month would begin`)) `days on which earlier periods of one month in respect of the same event began`))

-- Paragraph (4C): each period of one month begins on the date specified by the Secretary of State after the claimant has notified the
-- Secretary of State of the circumstances in paragraph (4A), provided the Secretary of State is satisfied that they apply. The date
-- specified is not required to be later than the notification (fork F-99-6).
-- src:1575 | (4C) Each period of one month begins on the date specified by the Secretary of State after the claimant has notified the Secretary of State of the circumstances in paragraph (4A) provided that the Secretary of State is satisfied that the circumstances apply.
@ref reg 99(4C) (src:1575)
GIVEN `the claimant has notified the Secretary of State of the circumstances in paragraph (4A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the circumstances apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date specified by the Secretary of State on which the period of one month begins` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(4C) — a period of one month under paragraph (4A) is running` `the claimant has notified the Secretary of State of the circumstances in paragraph (4A)` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the circumstances apply` `date specified by the Secretary of State on which the period of one month begins` `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    IF (`the claimant has notified the Secretary of State of the circumstances in paragraph (4A)`) AND (`the Secretary of State is satisfied that the circumstances apply`)
    THEN
        CONSIDER `date specified by the Secretary of State on which the period of one month begins`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST begins THEN
            ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day begins) AT LEAST 0)
            AND ((Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` begins (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 1, unit IS months))) LESS THAN 0)
    ELSE FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraphs (5), (5A) and (5B) — the Secretary of State is satisfied that a requirement is unreasonable`

-- Paragraph (5)(a): the claimant is carrying out a work preparation requirement or voluntary work preparation (as defined in regulation 95(4)).
-- out of range: sections 15 to 18 and 23 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which requirement is in question, and its limits, are stated inputs
-- src:1576 | (5) This paragraph applies where the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work search requirement ..., including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 17(4) ... of the Act, because ...—
-- src:1577 | (a) the claimant is carrying out a work preparation requirement or voluntary work preparation (as defined in regulation 95(4));
@ref reg 99(5)(a) (src:1576-1577)
GIVEN `the claimant is carrying out a work preparation requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `particular action taken by the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is agreed by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is for the purpose of making it more likely that the claimant will obtain paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is specified by the Secretary of State as a work preparation requirement under section 16 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(5)(a) — the claimant is carrying out a work preparation requirement or voluntary work preparation` `the claimant is carrying out a work preparation requirement` `particular action taken by the claimant` `the action is agreed by the Secretary of State` `the action is for the purpose of making it more likely that the claimant will obtain paid work` `the action is specified by the Secretary of State as a work preparation requirement under section 16 of the Act` MEANS
    `the claimant is carrying out a work preparation requirement`
    OR (`reg 95(4) — voluntary work preparation` `particular action taken by the claimant` `the action is agreed by the Secretary of State` `the action is for the purpose of making it more likely that the claimant will obtain paid work` `the action is specified by the Secretary of State as a work preparation requirement under section 16 of the Act`)

-- Paragraph (5)(b): the claimant has temporary child care responsibilities or is dealing with a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or
-- other temporary circumstances.
-- src:1578 | (b) the claimant has temporary child care responsibilities or is dealing with a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances; ...
@ref reg 99(5)(b) (src:1578)
GIVEN `the claimant has temporary child care responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is dealing with a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(5)(b) — the claimant has temporary child care responsibilities or is dealing with a temporary matter` `the claimant has temporary child care responsibilities` `the claimant is dealing with a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances` MEANS
    `the claimant has temporary child care responsibilities`
    OR `the claimant is dealing with a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances`

-- Paragraph (5)(c): the claimant is unfit for work for longer than the 14 days of paragraph (4)(a) or for more than 2 such periods in any
-- period of 12 months and, where requested by the Secretary of State, provides the evidence mentioned in paragraph (4)(b)(ii).
-- src:1579 | (c) the claimant is unfit for work for longer than the period of 14 days specified in paragraph (4)(a) or for more than 2 such periods in any period of 12 months and, where requested by the Secretary of State, provides the evidence mentioned in paragraph (4)(b)(ii) ; or
@ref reg 99(5)(c) (src:1579)
GIVEN facts IS AN `Unfitness for work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(5)(c) — the claimant is unfit for work for longer or for more periods than paragraph (4)(a) allows` facts MEANS
    `longer or more periods`
    AND (`reg 99(4)(b)(ii) — the evidence for any further days has been provided if requested` facts)
    WHERE
        `longer or more periods` MEANS
            ((facts's `days for which the claimant is unfit for work after the date that the evidence referred to in sub-paragraph (b) is provided`) GREATER THAN 14)
            OR ((facts's `number of such periods of unfitness for work in the period of 12 months, including this one`) GREATER THAN 2)

-- Paragraph (5)(d): paragraph (4) would apply to the claimant but for paragraph (4ZA).
-- src:1580 | (d) paragraph (4) would apply to the claimant but for paragraph (4ZA).
@ref reg 99(5)(d) (src:1580)
GIVEN facts IS AN `Unfitness for work facts`
      `paragraph (4ZB) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State makes a decision to carry out an assessment under regulation 41(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(5)(d) — paragraph (4) would apply but for paragraph (4ZA)` facts `paragraph (4ZB) applies` `the Secretary of State makes a decision to carry out an assessment under regulation 41(1)(b)` MEANS
    (`reg 99(4)(a) — the claimant is unfit for work for a period and number of periods within the limits` facts)
    AND (`reg 99(4)(b) — the claimant provides the evidence` facts)
    AND (NOT (`reg 99(4ZA) — paragraph (4) is open to the claimant` `paragraph (4ZB) applies` `the Secretary of State makes a decision to carry out an assessment under regulation 41(1)(b)`))

-- The claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph (5). The text of (5A) and (5B) uses this phrase.
@ref reg 99(5) (src:1576-1580)
GIVEN `sub-paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sub-paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sub-paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sub-paragraph (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(5) — the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)` `sub-paragraph (a)` `sub-paragraph (b)` `sub-paragraph (c)` `sub-paragraph (d)` MEANS
    `sub-paragraph (a)` OR `sub-paragraph (b)` OR `sub-paragraph (c)` OR `sub-paragraph (d)`

-- Paragraph (5): applies where the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a
-- work search requirement, including if limited under section 17(4) of the Act, because the claimant falls within one of the four
-- sub-paragraphs. Both the satisfaction and a sub-paragraph are needed (fork F-99-7).
-- out of range: sections 15 to 18 and 23 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which requirement is in question, and its limits, are stated inputs
@ref reg 99(5) (src:1576)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work search requirement, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 17(4) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(5) — this paragraph applies` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work search requirement, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 17(4) of the Act` `the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph (5)` MEANS
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work search requirement, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 17(4) of the Act`
    AND `the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph (5)`

-- Paragraph (5A): applies where the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a
-- work availability requirement to be able and willing to take up paid work and to attend an interview (including if limited under section
-- 18(3) of the Act) because the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph (5).
-- out of range: sections 15 to 18 and 23 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which requirement is in question, and its limits, are stated inputs
-- src:1581 | (5A) This paragraph applies where the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work availability requirement to be able and willing to—
-- src:1582 | (a) take up paid work; and
-- src:1583 | (b) attend an interview,
-- src:1584 | (including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 18(3) of the Act) because the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph (5).
@ref reg 99(5A) (src:1581-1584)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work availability requirement to be able and willing to take up paid work and to attend an interview, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 18(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(5A) — this paragraph applies` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work availability requirement to be able and willing to take up paid work and to attend an interview, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 18(3) of the Act` `the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph (5)` MEANS
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work availability requirement to be able and willing to take up paid work and to attend an interview, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 18(3) of the Act`
    AND `the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph (5)`

-- Paragraph (5B): applies where the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be (a) unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with
-- a work availability requirement to be able and willing to take up paid work because the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c)
-- or (d) of paragraph (5), and (b) reasonable to require compliance with a work availability requirement to be able and willing to attend
-- an interview, including if limited under section 18(3) of the Act.
-- out of range: sections 15 to 18 and 23 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which requirement is in question, and its limits, are stated inputs
-- src:1585 | (5B) This paragraph applies where the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be—
-- src:1586 | (a) unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work availability requirement to be able and willing to take up paid work because the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph (5); and
-- src:1587 | (b) reasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work availability requirement to be able and willing to attend an interview;
-- src:1588 | including if such requirement were limited in accordance with section 18(3) of the Act.
@ref reg 99(5B) (src:1585-1588)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work availability requirement to be able and willing to take up paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be reasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work availability requirement to be able and willing to attend an interview, including if such requirement were limited in accordance with section 18(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(5B) — this paragraph applies` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work availability requirement to be able and willing to take up paid work` `the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph (5)` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be reasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work availability requirement to be able and willing to attend an interview, including if such requirement were limited in accordance with section 18(3) of the Act` MEANS
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work availability requirement to be able and willing to take up paid work`
    AND `the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) of paragraph (5)`
    AND `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be reasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work availability requirement to be able and willing to attend an interview, including if such requirement were limited in accordance with section 18(3) of the Act`

