§§ `Paragraphs (6) and (6A) — earnings`

-- Paragraph (6)(a): the claimant has monthly earnings (excluding any that are not employed earnings, as defined in regulation 55 by
-- paragraph (6A)) equal to or more than the amount a person would be paid at the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage
-- Regulations for 18 hours a week, converted to a month by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12. Regulation 6(1A) disregards any fraction of
-- a pound in that amount, as for regulation 90. The earnings figure is compared as it stands (the same reading as in regulation 90).
-- out of range: regulations 4 and 4A of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (not among the inputs): the hourly rate is a stated input
-- out of range: regulation 55 (piece uc2): the earnings figure, excluding any that are not employed earnings, is a stated input
-- src:1589 | (6) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:1590 | (a) the claimant has monthly earnings (excluding any that are not employed earnings) that are equal to, or more than, the amount that a person would be paid at the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for 18 hours per week, converted to a monthly amount by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12; or
@ref reg 99(6)(a) (src:1589-1590)
GIVEN `the claimant's monthly earnings, excluding any that are not employed earnings (employed earnings as in regulation 55)` IS A NUMBER
      `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(6)(a) — the claimant's monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 18 hours` `the claimant's monthly earnings, excluding any that are not employed earnings (employed earnings as in regulation 55)` `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` MEANS
    `the claimant's monthly earnings, excluding any that are not employed earnings (employed earnings as in regulation 55)` AT LEAST (`reg 90 — the monthly amount paid for hours a week at an hourly rate, fraction of a pound disregarded` 18 `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`)

-- Paragraph (6)(b): the claimant is a member of a couple whose combined monthly earnings (excluding any that are not employed earnings)
-- are equal to or more than the amount for 29 hours a week.
-- out of range: regulations 4 and 4A of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (not among the inputs): the hourly rate is a stated input
-- out of range: regulation 55 (piece uc2): the earnings figure, excluding any that are not employed earnings, is a stated input
-- src:1591 | (b) the claimant is a member of a couple whose combined monthly earnings (excluding any that are not employed earnings) are equal to, or more than, the amount that a person would be paid at the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for 29 hours per week, converted to a monthly amount by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12.
-- src:1592 | (6A) In paragraph (6) “employed earnings” has the meaning in regulation 55.
@ref reg 99(6)(b) and (6A) (src:1591-1592)
GIVEN basis IS A `Claim basis`
      `the couple's combined monthly earnings, excluding any that are not employed earnings (employed earnings as in regulation 55)` IS A NUMBER
      `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(6)(b) — the couple's combined monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 29 hours` basis `the couple's combined monthly earnings, excluding any that are not employed earnings (employed earnings as in regulation 55)` `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` MEANS
    (`reg 2 — the claimant has a partner` basis)
    AND (`the couple's combined monthly earnings, excluding any that are not employed earnings (employed earnings as in regulation 55)` AT LEAST (`reg 90 — the monthly amount paid for hours a week at an hourly rate, fraction of a pound disregarded` 29 `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`))

@ref reg 99(6) (src:1589-1592)
GIVEN `limb (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(6) — this paragraph applies` `limb (a)` `limb (b)` MEANS
    `limb (a)` OR `limb (b)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraphs (1) to (2C) — what follows when a paragraph applies`

-- Paragraph (1)(a): where paragraph (3), (4), (4A) or (6) applies, the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement.
-- src:1529 | 99 Circumstances in which requirements must not be imposed
-- src:1530 | (1) Where paragraph (3), (4) , (4A), ... or (6) applies—
-- src:1531 | (a) the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement on a claimant; and
@ref reg 99(1)(a) (src:1529-1531)
GIVEN `paragraph (3) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (4A) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (6) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(1)(a) — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement` `paragraph (3) applies` `paragraph (4) applies` `paragraph (4A) applies` `paragraph (6) applies` MEANS
    `paragraph (3) applies` OR `paragraph (4) applies` OR `paragraph (4A) applies` OR `paragraph (6) applies`

-- Paragraph (1)(b): "able and willing immediately to take up work" under a work availability requirement means able and willing to take up
-- paid work, or attend an interview, immediately once the circumstances in paragraph (3), (4), (4A) or (6) no longer apply. When none of those
-- paragraphs applies, this paragraph says nothing about the meaning, so the rule returns NOTHING.
-- src:1532 | (b) “able and willing immediately to take up work” under a work availability requirement means able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, immediately once the circumstances set out in paragraph (3), (4) , (4A), ... or (6) no longer apply.
@ref reg 99(1)(b) (src:1532)
GIVEN `any of paragraphs (3), (4), (4A) and (6) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, immediately once those circumstances no longer apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 99(1)(b) — the claimant is able and willing immediately to take up work` `any of paragraphs (3), (4), (4A) and (6) applies` `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, immediately once those circumstances no longer apply` MEANS
    IF `any of paragraphs (3), (4), (4A) and (6) applies`
    THEN JUST `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, immediately once those circumstances no longer apply`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Paragraph (2): a work search requirement previously applying to the claimant ceases to have effect from the date on which the
-- circumstances in paragraph (3), (4), (4A) or (6) begin to apply. NOTHING for the date means the circumstances have not begun.
-- src:1533 | (2) A work search requirement previously applying to the claimant ceases to have effect from the date on which the circumstances set out in paragraph (3), (4) , (4A), ... or (6) begin to apply.
@ref reg 99(2) (src:1533)
GIVEN `date on which the circumstances in paragraph (3), (4), (4A) or (6) began to apply` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(2) — a work search requirement previously applying has ceased to have effect` `date on which the circumstances in paragraph (3), (4), (4A) or (6) began to apply` `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `date on which the circumstances in paragraph (3), (4), (4A) or (6) began to apply`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST began THEN (Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day began) AT LEAST 0

-- Paragraph (2A)(a): where paragraph (5) applies, the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement.
-- src:1534 | (2A) Where paragraph (5) applies—
-- src:1535 | (a) the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement on a claimant;
-- src:1536 | and
@ref reg 99(2A)(a) (src:1534-1536)
GIVEN `paragraph (5) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(2A)(a) — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement` `paragraph (5) applies` MEANS
    `paragraph (5) applies`

-- Paragraph (2A)(b): a work search requirement previously applying ceases to have effect from the date on which the circumstances in
-- paragraph (5) begin to apply.
-- src:1537 | (b) a work search requirement previously applying to the claimant ceases to have effect from the date on which the circumstances set out in paragraph (5) begin to apply.
@ref reg 99(2A)(b) (src:1537)
GIVEN `date on which the circumstances in paragraph (5) began to apply` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date as at which it is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 99(2A)(b) — a work search requirement previously applying has ceased to have effect` `date on which the circumstances in paragraph (5) began to apply` `the date as at which it is asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `date on which the circumstances in paragraph (5) began to apply`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST began THEN (Day `the date as at which it is asked` MINUS Day began) AT LEAST 0

-- Paragraph (2B): where paragraph (5A) applies, "able and willing to take up work" means able and willing to take up paid work, or to attend
-- an interview, immediately once the circumstances in paragraph (5A) no longer apply. NOTHING when (5A) does not apply.
-- src:1538 | (2B) Where paragraph (5A) applies “able and willing to take up work” under a work availability requirement means able and willing to take up paid work, or to attend an interview, immediately once the circumstances set out in paragraph (5A) no longer apply.
@ref reg 99(2B) (src:1538)
GIVEN `paragraph (5A) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or to attend an interview, immediately once the circumstances in paragraph (5A) no longer apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 99(2B) — the claimant is able and willing to take up work` `paragraph (5A) applies` `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or to attend an interview, immediately once the circumstances in paragraph (5A) no longer apply` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (5A) applies`
    THEN JUST `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work, or to attend an interview, immediately once the circumstances in paragraph (5A) no longer apply`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Paragraph (2C): where paragraph (5B) applies, "able and willing to take up work" means (a) able and willing to take up paid work
-- immediately once the circumstances in paragraph (5B) no longer apply, and (b) able and willing to attend an interview before those
-- circumstances no longer apply. NOTHING when (5B) does not apply.
-- src:1539 | (2C) Where paragraph (5B) applies, “able and willing to take up work” under a work availability requirement means—
-- src:1540 | (a) able and willing to take up paid work immediately once the circumstances set out in paragraph (5B) no longer apply; and
-- src:1541 | (b) able and willing to attend an interview before those circumstances no longer apply.
@ref reg 99(2C) (src:1539-1541)
GIVEN `paragraph (5B) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work immediately once the circumstances in paragraph (5B) no longer apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is able and willing to attend an interview before those circumstances no longer apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 99(2C) — the claimant is able and willing to take up work` `paragraph (5B) applies` `the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work immediately once the circumstances in paragraph (5B) no longer apply` `the claimant is able and willing to attend an interview before those circumstances no longer apply` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (5B) applies`
    THEN JUST ((`the claimant is able and willing to take up paid work immediately once the circumstances in paragraph (5B) no longer apply`) AND (`the claimant is able and willing to attend an interview before those circumstances no longer apply`))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Composite: no work search requirement may be imposed if paragraph (3), (4), (4A) or (6) applies (paragraph (1)(a)), or paragraph (5)
-- applies (paragraph (2A)(a)).
@ref reg 99(1)(a) (src:1531)
